text:
A conventional bank licensee must take reasonable steps to provide
periodic training and information to ensure that staff who handle
customer transactions, or are managerially responsible for such
transactions, are made aware of:
(a) Their responsibilities under the AML Law, this Module, and any
other relevant AML / CFT laws and regulations;
(b) The identity and responsibilities of the MLRO and his deputy;
(c) The potential consequences, both individual and corporate, of any
breach of the AML Law, this Module and any other relevant AML
/ CFT laws or regulations;
(d) The conventional bank licensee's current AML/CFT policies and
procedures;
(e) Money laundering and terrorist financing typologies and trends;
(f) The type of customer activity or transaction that may justify an
internal STR;
(g) The conventional bank licensee's procedures for making internal
STRs; and
(h) Customer due diligence measures with respect to establishing
business relations with customers.

